Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:27:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Swift: Flatten the brain behaviour loop

Brain#startEachNonRunningBehavior and #getRunningBehaviors walked a
TreeMap -> HashMap -> LinkedHashSet nest for every mob every tick. Keep a
snapshot of that nest in its own iteration order (rebuilt whenever a
behaviour is added or all are removed) as (activity, behaviours[]) groups,
and check each group's activity live when the group is reached, exactly as
the nested walk does (a starting behaviour can change the active
activities for later groups). Duplicates across activities are kept.

-Dswift.verify=true runs vanilla's walk authoritatively with the snapshot
in lockstep (same group, same activity decision, same behaviours) and
reports any difference. Disable with -Dswift.flatBrainLoop=false.

Benchmark: villager brain tick 4.1 -> 2.6 us (1.5-1.6x).

